# Castlevania: Curse of Darkness (4B4E002D), FIRST RUN: no save on the disk.
# PLAYED by nav.py on the Nova, 2026-10-01 14:18 PDT (lane.titleroutes HELD
# session castlevania-cod.first-run-20261001T141851, the owner-approved
# one-time Nova path-finding session, #397).
#
# Replaces the two earlier drafts, neither ever played past a menu:
# lane.routeprep's all-[guess] draft (adopted session 42, never replayed) and
# the generic `--route survey`-derived castlevania-cod.route (session 48,
# Thor, heat-stopped at 284/300s, never confirmed by a real replay). The
# trap both missed: NEW GAME's Name Entry keyboard needs an explicit jump to
# "Accept" (press START, which jumps the cursor there on this keyboard; A
# alone leaves the cursor on the letter grid), and the save-data prompt
# right after defaults its cursor to "No" (axis LX min moves it onto "Yes"
# before A, or the route declines its own save and loops back to Name
# Entry).
#
#   intro FMV (A) -> title, New Game (A) -> Name Entry: A types the
#   highlighted "A", START jumps the cursor to Accept, A accepts -> "Is this
#   correct?" (A, Yes already selected) -> "There is no save data... Create
#   new save data?" (LX min moves the cursor from the default No onto Yes,
#   then A) -> "Creating new save data..." -> save slot list, slot 1
#   highlighted (A) -> "Saving..." -> the opening cutscene (1476, Valachia;
#   A three times, 5.4s apart, clears the castle-exterior shots) -> player
#   control in a gothic courtyard facing a gargoyle fountain.
#
# Player control confirmed by eye: LY min visibly closed the distance to the
# fountain between two shots taken 1.5s apart (014-moved.png), then the play
# pattern (LY min/press A/RX sweep) walked him along the fountain's edge and
# into an attack animation (016-postplay.png). HP bar steady at 100/100
# throughout -- no combat pressure this early.
#
# REPLAYED UNATTENDED, FAILED TWICE on the newgame->Name-Entry transition,
# not a step-ordering bug: the load time between selecting NEW GAME and the
# Name Entry keyboard becoming interactive varies by 10+ seconds between
# runs (confirmed by the owner from a THIRD run, see below).
#
#   - session 59 (#397, dispatch 1790902028-titleroutes-1005086, Nova): a
#     single "press A, wait 1.1, shot name-a" step landed on a still-black
#     screen (174838-name-a.png empty) that the interactive authoring
#     session's identical timing had landed on a loaded one
#     (003-name-a.png, field shows "A"). Session 59's fix -- a second blind
#     press 4s later -- assumed the SCREEN was up and only the PRESS had
#     been dropped.
#   - That fix was wrong in exactly the way the owner called out (ADDENDUM
#     11, 2026-10-01 ~18:30 PDT, request 1790903439-titleroutes-1317193,
#     stopped mid-run): both `name-a` (181831) and `name-a2` (181838) are
#     STILL BLACK -- the screen had not loaded by either press, so both
#     presses went nowhere, and the route's later blind presses (meant for
#     slot selection etc.) typed into the keyboard once it finally came up,
#     leaving the name field reading "AAIIIIII" with no Accept
#     (182106-a5.png) for the rest of the 900s. A second blind press "a
#     timing error of that size" cannot fix, in the owner's words.
#
# FIXED FOR REAL this time: `waitfor` blocks until the Name Entry screen's
# own banner is actually on screen (so a 10s-plus load never gets typed
# into), then `press-until` presses A and checks the name field itself,
# retrying rather than guessing a fixed number of blind presses. See
# route.sh's grammar comment for how these compare screencaps.
# Reference crops: routes/refs/castlevania-cod.first-run/name-entry-header.png
# (the "Name Entry" banner, scratch/nav/castlevania-cod.first-run-20261001T141851/002-newgame.png)
# and .../name-field-empty.png (the empty name field, same frame). Selftest:
# `python3 docs/testing/titles/waitfor_selftest.py` (checked against fixture
# crops of this exact screen, including the still-black frame above, under
# `routes/refs/castlevania-cod.first-run/selftest/`).
wait 10.9
shot boot
wait 13.4
press A
wait 5.8
shot a1
wait 10.3
press A
waitfor name-entry-header 30 50,65,490,85 15
shot newgame
press-until A name-field-empty 5 1.5 350,180,120,70 8
shot name-a
wait 1
press START
wait 1.1
shot name-start
wait 7.6
press A
wait 2.1
shot accepted
wait 6.7
press A
wait 3.1
shot yes
wait 11.2
axis LX min
wait 0.5
axis LX mid
wait 1.1
shot left1
wait 8.5
press A
wait 4.1
shot createdsave
wait 12.1
shot wait5
wait 8.3
press A
wait 4.1
shot slot1
wait 13.4
shot saved1
wait 18.7
press A
wait 5.1
shot a2
wait 7.5
press A
wait 5.4
press A
wait 5.4
press A
wait 5.7
shot a5
wait 9.0
axis LY min
wait 1.7
axis LY mid
shot moved
wait 7.2
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    axis LY min
    wait 2
    press A
    axis RX max
    wait 0.5
    axis RX mid
    axis LY mid
    wait 1
    press A
    wait 2
}
